{
  "_comment": [
    "How each hand-curated table file maps onto assay ids. gc bundle melts the wide published",
    "tables into long-format measurements.csv using only this file, so a paper with a completely",
    "different assay panel needs no code change: it needs its own tables.json.",
    "keys are the identity columns; every other named column becomes one measurement row.",
    "Columns absent from `columns` are ignored, which is how entry numbers stay out of the data."
  ],
  "tables": [
